ate and peer-call limits are set.\n29\t\n30\t`config/budgets.yaml` lines 1–15 (cited lines marked >):\n31\t```\n32\t   1  # Hard limits enforced by src/agent/budget.ts, outside the model.\n33\t   2  run:\n34\t   3>   maxTurns: 8                 # model calls per run\n35\t   4    maxWallMs: 45000            # whole run, including tool calls\n36\t   5    maxInputTokens: 120000      # summed across model calls in the run\n37\t   6    maxOutputTokens: 6000\n38\t   7    maxCostUsd: 0.40\n39\t   8    maxToolCalls: 16\n40\t   9    maxToolCallsPerMinute: 12\n41\t  10    maxPeerCalls: 2             # calls to the eligibility agent; this agent starts no sub-agents\n42\t  11  \n43\t  12  quotas:\n44\t  13    # Daily spend and per-minute tool-call ceilings across many runs.\n45\t  14    perSubjectDailyUsd: 2.00    # one patient or staff user\n46\t  15    perTenantDailyUsd: 60.00    # one clinic\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\t## B07.2\n50\t\n51\t**Check:** The harness or a gateway outside the model enforces each limit and stops or escalates the run when it is hit; the model cannot raise, reset, or skip them.\n52\t\n53\t**How to verify:** 1) For each limit, find the code that enforces it and what happens when hit. 2) Check it runs in the harness or gateway. 3) Answer no if a limit is only in the prompt, can be changed by a tool argument or model output, is caught and the run continues, or hitting it has no stop or escalation.\n54\t\n55\t**Reviewer's evidence:** src/agent/budget.ts:102 — \"if (used > max) {\"\n56\t\n57\t**Reviewer's note:** The harness throws and aborts when a limit is passed; the run stops and hands off to staff.\n58\t\n59\t`src/agent/budget.ts` lines 90–114 (cited lines marked >):\n60\t```\n61\t  90      );\n62\t  91    }\n63\t  92  \n64\t  93    get signal(): AbortSignal {\n65\t  94      return this.abort.signal;\n66\t  95    }\n67\t  96  \n68\t  97    dispose(): void {\n69\t  98      clearTimeout(this.timer);\n70\t  99    }\n71\t 100  \n72\t 101    private check(limit: L