{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdgDEh9gmvVixPPnReMd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with an overall verdict of **failed**. B07.1, B07.2 and B07.3 hold. B07.4 fails.\n\n- **B07.4 (fails):** the daily spend and per-minute tool-call quotas in DynamoDB are only charged from `recordUsage` and `toolCall`. The intent classifier call at `loop.ts:41` runs on every request before any of that, so its cost never counts toward the subject, tenant or fleet quotas. The `count_tokens` call at `loop.ts:60` isn't counted either. Nothing in `sms-webhook.ts` or `webchat.ts` rate limits run starts. Many short runs routed to staff can therefore use model capacity with no quota applied.\n- **`violates`:** I copied two phrases from the requirement into it: \"set spend and rate quotas per user or service, per tenant, and across the whole fleet\" and \"many small runs can't use up shared capacity\".\n- **B07.1–B07.3:** all six per-run limits have finite values. `RunBudget` aborts the run and throws when a limit is hit, and `loop.ts` stops the run and hands off to staff. The agent starts no sub-agents, and its calls to the eligibility agent are capped at 2.\n\nI didn't run any code, and I only wrote `verdict.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1613,"cache_read_input_tokens":29680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1613},"output_tokens":438,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6502f0a5-c0a7-41a6-9b02-2168e30d8e06","uuid":"33139264-6c37-4995-becf-8c2578715e53","timestamp":"2026-10-02T15:51:04.184Z","request_id":"req_011CfdgDDumMu6tX4eJYeP3R"}
